((date 2026-09-13) (slug stop-width-12pct-weekly-cadence-v10dedup)
 (hypothesis
  "The 09-05 stop-width x cadence surface's both-window survivor - initial_stop_buffer 0.9167 (12% initial width) + stop_update_cadence Weekly (trail re-evaluated on the week's final bar, trigger still continuous) - beats the record convention on the 26y top-3000 PIT-2000 window when re-measured on the deduped warehouse and the fixed exit basis. Prior evidence (sw26y-w12-W-s0 = 761% / maxDD 29.7) was on the OLD exit basis and the twin-carrying _v7mark warehouse, both since shown to invert or inflate reads (project_lever_reads_invert_on_fixed_sim, project_stop_buffer_by_macro_state_axis).")
 (base_scenario
  "cadence-12w-v10-2026-09-13: arm a4 = the a0-breadth-on-null spec (record convention + breadth_direction ON) + ((initial_stop_buffer 0.9167)) ((stop_update_cadence Weekly)), salts 0/1/2 on _v10dedup 2000 (build 31e4bb9c3, pinned worktree sweep-detgate), paired against the committed a0-v10 null cells of stop-width-by-state-2026-09-08 (build 969637974). Pairing gate validator_diff -check V6: exit 0 at salt 0; DIFFER at salts 1/2 on ONE arm-only pair (IAC/MTCH 2006-03-16 -> 03-20, a spin-off backfill twin the rename-twin dedupe does not model, #2782; duplicated leg -$2.7k / -$2.9k on +$1.97M / +$2.48M realised deltas) - read ex-twin with the mismatch on record. Pre-registered binary rule (same as item 3's): realised P&L AND maxDD both better at >= 2 of 3 salts.")
 (window_id top3000-2000-2026-record-26y-3salt) (baseline_label record-breadth-on-null-v10dedup)
